Line 13: This First Amendment (this \"Amendment\") to the Amended and Restated Agreement of Limited Partnership of Solara Digital Partners Fund V LP, a Delaware limited partnership (the \"Partnership\" or \"Fund V\"), is entered into as of \[●\], 2025 (the \"Effective Date\"), by and among Solara Digital Infrastructure GP LLC, a Delaware limited liability company, as general partner of the Partnership (the \"General Partner\" or \"Solara GP\"), and the limited partners of the Partnership (collectively, the \"Limited Partners\" and, together with the General Partner, the \"Partners\").
Line 45: **WHEREAS**, the LP Advisory Committee (the \"LPAC\") of the Partnership met on April 22, 2025, and, following a presentation by the General Partner and review of materials prepared by Calderwood & Harkness LLP and Whitfield, Carruthers & Doyle LLP, provided preliminary consent to the Reorganization, with Limited Partners holding approximately 78% in interest of the capital commitments to the Partnership voting in favor of the Reorganization;
Line 47: **WHEREAS**, the Reorganization is motivated by the following considerations: (i) operational cost reduction --- the Solara platform currently incurs approximately \$3,800,000 annually in duplicative offshore administration, audit, regulatory filing, and compliance fees across the parallel fund structures, which costs are expected to be materially reduced through consolidation; (ii) the impact of forthcoming Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (\"OECD\") Pillar Two Global Anti-Base Erosion (\"GloBE\") rules, which become effective for the Luxembourg SCSp entities from fiscal year 2025 and which diminish certain tax benefits that were originally expected to be derived from the Luxembourg structures; (iii) simplified compliance under the Foreign Account Tax Compliance Act (\"FATCA\") (IRC §§ 1471--1474) and the Common Reporting Standard (\"CRS\") reporting requirements, enabling more efficient tax information exchange across the Solara platform; and (iv) LP-requested governance simplification, as multiple Limited Partners have expressed a preference for a streamlined fund structure that reduces complexity in reporting, distributions, and investment monitoring;
Line 49: **WHEREAS**, the Reorganization involves the domestication and effective merger of the Cayman Islands and Luxembourg parallel fund vehicles into a newly established Delaware-domiciled master fund structure, specifically involving the formation and utilization of the following new entities:
Line 59: > **Step 1** (target effective date: September 15, 2025) --- Formation of the Master Fund GP, the Consolidated Master Fund, the International Feeder, and the Tax-Exempt Feeder, including the filing of certificates of formation and certificates of limited partnership with the Delaware Secretary of State for the Delaware entities and the registration of the Cayman entities with the Cayman Islands Monetary Authority, and the filing of Internal Revenue Service Form 8832 entity classification elections (check-the-box elections) for each new entity to be classified as a partnership for U.S. federal income tax purposes under Treasury Regulations § 301.7701-3;
Line 61: > **Step 2** (target effective date: October 1, 2025) --- Contribution by Solara Digital Partners Fund IV-A (Cayman) LP (\"Fund IV-A Cayman\") of all of its portfolio company assets (aggregate fair market value of \$2,310,000,000; adjusted tax basis of \$1,620,000,000; built-in gain of \$690,000,000) to the Consolidated Master Fund in exchange for a limited partnership interest in the Consolidated Master Fund;
Line 63: > **Step 3** (target effective date: October 15, 2025) --- Contribution by Solara Digital Partners Fund IV-B (Luxembourg) SCSp (\"Fund IV-B Lux\") of all of its portfolio company assets (aggregate fair market value of €1,070,000,000 / approximately \$1,160,000,000; adjusted tax basis of €782,000,000 / approximately \$844,600,000; built-in gain of €288,000,000 / approximately \$311,000,000) to the Consolidated Master Fund in exchange for a limited partnership interest in the Consolidated Master Fund;
Line 65: > **Step 4** (target effective date: November 1, 2025) --- Contribution by Fund V-A Cayman of all of its portfolio company assets (aggregate fair market value of \$2,890,000,000; adjusted tax basis of \$2,340,000,000; built-in gain of \$550,000,000) to the Consolidated Master Fund in exchange for a limited partnership interest in the Consolidated Master Fund, and contribution by Fund V-B Lux of all of its portfolio company assets (aggregate fair market value of €1,290,000,000 / approximately \$1,390,000,000; adjusted tax basis of €1,140,000,000 / approximately \$1,230,000,000; built-in gain of €150,000,000 / approximately \$162,000,000) to the Consolidated Master Fund in exchange for a limited partnership interest in the Consolidated Master Fund; and
Line 67: > **Step 5** (target effective date: December 1, 2025) --- Dissolution of Fund V-A Cayman and Fund V-B Lux (along with Fund IV-A Cayman and Fund IV-B Lux) and distribution of their respective limited partnership interests in the Consolidated Master Fund to their existing limited partners, with non-U.S. limited partners rolling into the International Feeder and U.S. tax-exempt limited partners rolling into the Tax-Exempt Feeder;
Line 75: **WHEREAS**, Whitfield, Carruthers & Doyle LLP (Diana Carruthers, Partner) serves as outside counsel to the LPAC and has reviewed the proposed Reorganization for LP consent purposes and has provided the LPAC with an independent assessment of the potential risks, benefits, and alternatives associated with the Reorganization;
Line 79: **WHEREAS**, the Partnership Agreement requires the consent of the Limited Partners holding a specified percentage in interest of capital commitments for certain amendments to the Partnership Agreement and for certain significant transactions, and this Amendment is being submitted to the Limited Partners for their approval in accordance with such requirements;
Line 109: \"**Reorganization Documents**\" means, collectively, all agreements, instruments, certificates, consents, elections, filings, and other documents to be executed, delivered, and filed in connection with the Reorganization, including, without limitation, the limited partnership agreement of the Consolidated Master Fund, the operating agreement of the Master Fund GP, the limited partnership agreements of the International Feeder and the Tax-Exempt Feeder, contribution agreements, assignment and assumption agreements, Form 8832 entity classification elections, the PLR Request, lender consent letters, insurance endorsements, and any other documents reasonably necessary to consummate the Reorganization.
Line 121: \(b\) In the event of any conflict or inconsistency between the terms and provisions of this Amendment and the terms and provisions of the Partnership Agreement (as in effect immediately prior to the effectiveness of this Amendment), the terms and provisions of this Amendment shall control and prevail.
Line 129: **Section 2.1 --- Consent to the Reorganization**
Line 131: The Limited Partners hereby consent to the Reorganization as described in the Recitals to this Amendment, including, without limitation, the following actions:
Line 133: > \(a\) The contribution by Fund V-A Cayman and Fund V-B Lux of all of their respective portfolio company assets to the Consolidated Master Fund in exchange for limited partnership interests therein, as contemplated by Step 4 of the Reorganization (target effective date: November 1, 2025);
Line 135: > \(b\) The dissolution of Fund V-A Cayman and Fund V-B Lux and the distribution of their respective partnership interests in the Consolidated Master Fund to their respective limited partners, as contemplated by Step 5 of the Reorganization (target effective date: December 1, 2025);
Line 139: > \(d\) The establishment of the post-Reorganization structure whereby Fund V LP will co-invest directly alongside the Consolidated Master Fund on a proportionate basis, rather than alongside separate parallel offshore vehicles, in a manner designed to preserve the economic rights, investment exposure, and proportionate sharing of gains, losses, and distributions applicable to the Limited Partners.
Line 141: The consent of the Limited Partners provided pursuant to this Section 2.1 is granted with the understanding that the Reorganization is subject to the conditions precedent set forth in Article V of this Amendment and that the General Partner retains the authority to modify the timing and structure of the Reorganization steps as provided in Section 2.4.
Line 149: > \(b\) **Negotiation and Execution of Reorganization Documents.** Negotiate, execute, and deliver the limited partnership agreement of the Consolidated Master Fund, the operating agreement of the Master Fund GP, the limited partnership agreements of the International Feeder and the Tax-Exempt Feeder, and all other Reorganization Documents, on such terms and conditions as the General Partner determines in its reasonable discretion to be in the best interests of the Partnership and the Limited Partners;
Line 151: > \(c\) **Entity Classification Elections.** File Internal Revenue Service Form 8832 (Entity Classification Election) for the Consolidated Master Fund, the International Feeder, and the Tax-Exempt Feeder, in each case electing classification as a partnership for U.S. federal income tax purposes under Treasury Regulations § 301.7701-3, and take all actions necessary to ensure the timely filing and effectiveness of such elections;
Line 159: > \(g\) **Asset Contributions and Reorganization Steps.** Cause the contribution of Fund V parallel vehicle portfolio company assets to the Consolidated Master Fund and take all actions necessary or advisable to consummate Steps 4 and 5 of the Reorganization, including the execution of contribution agreements, assignment and assumption agreements, and instruments of transfer;
Line 165: > \(j\) **Lender Consents.** Execute amendments, consents, and waivers under existing credit facilities as necessary to permit the consummation of the Reorganization, including obtaining consent from Ashford National Bank, N.A. (Thomas Greenleaf, Managing Director, Fund Finance) and Sentinel Capital Markets LLC (Laura Pak, Vice President) under the Partnership\'s \$1,500,000,000 Fund V subscription revolving credit facility, and negotiate such modifications to the credit facility documentation as may be required to reflect the post-Reorganization structure;
Line 175: > \(o\) **General Authority.** Take all other actions as may be reasonably necessary, appropriate, or desirable to consummate the Reorganization, including the execution and delivery of any additional agreements, instruments, certificates, consents, and filings, and the engagement of additional advisors, service providers, and professionals as the General Partner may determine in its reasonable discretion to be necessary or advisable.
Line 195: > \(h\) **No IRC § 1446 Withholding.** No withholding under IRC § 1446(a) is required with respect to the Step 4 Contributions or the Step 5 distributions, as the Step 4 Contributions are tax-free contributions that do not give rise to effectively connected taxable income allocable to foreign partners, and the Step 5 distributions are tax-free distributions under IRC § 731(a).
Line 203: The authorization granted to the General Partner pursuant to this Article II extends to actions taken prior to, on, or after the Effective Date in furtherance of the Reorganization. Any actions taken by the General Partner prior to the Effective Date that were within the scope of the authorization granted by this Article II are hereby ratified and confirmed.
Line 205: The General Partner may modify the timing of the Reorganization steps described in the Recitals, provided that the target effective date for the Step 5 Dissolutions remains on or about December 1, 2025, or such other date as the General Partner determines in its reasonable discretion, taking into account the progress of the PLR Request, the receipt of lender consents, the availability of regulatory approvals, and other relevant factors. The General Partner shall provide the LPAC with reasonable advance notice of any material changes to the Reorganization timeline.
Line 207: The General Partner may adjust the structure of the Reorganization as reasonably necessary to address feedback received from the IRS during the pre-submission conference (which has been requested for July 22, 2025) or in response to the PLR Request, or to address changes in applicable tax law, regulation, or administrative guidance, provided that such adjustments do not materially adversely affect the economic rights, investment exposure, or tax position of the Limited Partners. If any structural adjustment is required that would, in the General Partner\'s reasonable judgment, materially adversely affect the Limited Partners, the General Partner shall seek LPAC consent prior to implementing such adjustment.
Line 241: The transfer restrictions and withdrawal provisions in the Partnership Agreement are hereby amended to permit the limited partner migration contemplated in Step 5 of the Reorganization without requiring the individual transfer consent procedures that would otherwise apply under the Partnership Agreement. Specifically:
Line 243: > \(a\) The migration of non-U.S. limited partners from Fund V-A Cayman to the International Feeder shall not be treated as a \"transfer\" requiring the General Partner\'s consent or the satisfaction of any other transfer conditions under the Partnership Agreement; and
Line 245: > \(b\) The migration of U.S. tax-exempt limited partners from Fund V-A Cayman and Fund V-B Lux to the Tax-Exempt Feeder shall not be treated as a \"transfer\" requiring the General Partner\'s consent or the satisfaction of any other transfer conditions under the Partnership Agreement.
Line 247: Any admission of a Limited Partner or former limited partner of the Legacy Offshore Vehicles into the International Feeder or the Tax-Exempt Feeder in connection with the Reorganization shall not be treated as a new admission, a transfer, or a secondary transaction requiring consent under the Partnership Agreement. For all purposes of the Partnership Agreement and the Reorganization Documents, such migrations and admissions shall be treated as part of the integrated Reorganization transaction and shall not give rise to any transfer fees, consent fees, or other charges that might otherwise be assessed in connection with transfers or admissions under the Partnership Agreement.
Line 261: **Section 3.6 --- Amendment to LPAC Provisions**
Line 263: The LPAC provisions of the Partnership Agreement are hereby amended to reflect that the LPAC\'s oversight and consent authority extends to matters involving the Consolidated Master Fund, the International Feeder, and the Tax-Exempt Feeder insofar as such matters affect the Partnership, the Limited Partners, or the economic terms of their investment in the Partnership.
Line 265: Whitfield, Carruthers & Doyle LLP (Diana Carruthers, Partner) shall continue to serve as outside counsel to the LPAC and shall provide independent advice to the LPAC with respect to matters arising under the Consolidated Master Fund structure and the feeder vehicles.
Line 267: The preliminary consent provided by the LPAC at the meeting held on April 22, 2025, at which Limited Partners holding approximately 78% in interest of the capital commitments to the Partnership voted in favor of the Reorganization, is hereby confirmed and ratified. Such consent shall be deemed to satisfy any LPAC consent requirements under the Partnership Agreement with respect to the Reorganization, including the formation of the new entities, the Step 4 Contributions, the Step 5 Dissolutions, and the related limited partner migrations.
Line 279: The General Partner hereby represents and warrants to the Limited Partners as of the Effective Date as follows:
Line 283: > \(b\) **Due Authorization.** The execution and delivery of this Amendment by the General Partner and the consummation of the Reorganization have been duly authorized by all necessary limited liability company action on the part of the General Partner, including the approval of the board of the General Partner obtained at a duly convened meeting held on March 14, 2025, and no further action on the part of the General Partner is required to authorize this Amendment or the Reorganization.
Line 287: > \(d\) **No Violation.** The execution and delivery of this Amendment and the consummation of the Reorganization will not (i) violate any provision of the organizational documents of the General Partner, the Partnership, or any Legacy Offshore Vehicle, (ii) violate any applicable law, statute, rule, regulation, order, judgment, or decree of any governmental authority, (iii) result in a breach of, or default under, any material agreement, contract, or instrument to which the Partnership or the General Partner is a party or by which any of their respective assets are bound, or (iv) result in the creation or imposition of any lien, encumbrance, or security interest on any assets of the Partnership.
Line 291: > \(f\) **Lender Consents.** The General Partner will obtain all required consents under the Partnership\'s \$1,500,000,000 Fund V subscription revolving credit facility from Ashford National Bank, N.A. (Thomas Greenleaf, Managing Director, Fund Finance) and Sentinel Capital Markets LLC (Laura Pak, Vice President) prior to the consummation of Step 4 of the Reorganization. The General Partner has no reason to believe that such consents will not be obtained on a timely basis and on terms acceptable to the General Partner.
Line 297: Each Limited Partner, by executing the Form of LP Consent attached hereto as Exhibit A or otherwise consenting to this Amendment in the manner specified in the Partnership Agreement, hereby represents and warrants as of the date of such execution or consent as follows:
Line 299: > \(a\) **Authority.** Such Limited Partner has the requisite power and authority (corporate, partnership, trust, or otherwise, as applicable) to execute and deliver the Form of LP Consent and to consent to this Amendment and the Reorganization, and such execution, delivery, and consent have been duly authorized by all necessary action on the part of such Limited Partner.
Line 307: **Section 5.1 --- Conditions to Effectiveness of the Reorganization**
Line 309: The obligations of the General Partner to consummate the Reorganization (but not the effectiveness of this Amendment itself, which shall become effective upon its execution by the General Partner and the receipt of LP consent as provided herein) are subject to the satisfaction or waiver (in accordance with Section 5.2) of the following conditions:
Line 311: > \(a\) **LP Consent.** Receipt of consent to this Amendment and the Reorganization from Limited Partners holding at least the percentage in interest of capital commitments required under the Partnership Agreement for amendments and major transactions of the type contemplated hereby;
Line 315: > \(c\) **Entity Classification Elections.** Filing and effectiveness of Internal Revenue Service Form 8832 entity classification elections for each of the newly formed entities, electing partnership classification under Treasury Regulations § 301.7701-3;
Line 317: > \(d\) **Lender Consents.** Receipt of all required consents and waivers under the Partnership\'s \$1,500,000,000 Fund V subscription revolving credit facility from Ashford National Bank, N.A. and Sentinel Capital Markets LLC, on terms reasonably satisfactory to the General Partner;
Line 321: > \(f\) **No Material Adverse Tax Law Change.** No material adverse change in applicable U.S. federal income tax law, Treasury Regulations, IRS guidance, or judicial interpretation that would materially affect the intended tax-free treatment of the Reorganization as described in Section 2.3 of this Amendment shall have occurred between the Effective Date and the consummation of the relevant Reorganization step;
Line 331: The General Partner may, in its sole and absolute discretion, waive any one or more of the conditions precedent set forth in Section 5.1 at any time, except that the conditions set forth in Section 5.1(a) (LP Consent) and Section 5.1(f) (No Material Adverse Tax Law Change) may not be waived by the General Partner. Any waiver of a condition precedent by the General Partner shall not constitute a waiver of any other condition or any right of the General Partner under this Amendment or the Partnership Agreement.
Line 339: Without limiting the generality of the foregoing, the indemnification and exculpation provisions of the Partnership Agreement shall extend to, and shall apply with respect to, all actions taken and decisions made by the General Partner, its affiliates, and their respective officers, directors, managers, members, employees, and agents in connection with the Reorganization, including, without limitation, the negotiation, execution, and delivery of the Reorganization Documents, the formation of the new entities, the submission and prosecution of the PLR Request, the Step 4 Contributions, the Step 5 Dissolutions, and all other actions taken in furtherance of the Reorganization.
Line 343: To the extent not already covered by the indemnification and exculpation provisions of the Partnership Agreement, the Partnership shall indemnify and hold harmless the General Partner and its officers, directors, managers, members, and employees, including Viktor Raines (Managing Partner and Founder), Meredith Tsao (Chief Operating Officer), Douglas Wexford (Chief Financial Officer), Priya Narasimhan (General Counsel), and Stefan Dalmqvist (Head of Tax), from and against any and all losses, claims, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys\' fees and expenses of investigation and litigation) arising out of or relating to the Reorganization, the execution and delivery of this Amendment and the Reorganization Documents, the submission and prosecution of the PLR Request, and the consummation of the transactions contemplated hereby, except to the extent that such losses, claims, damages, liabilities, costs, or expenses are finally determined by a court of competent jurisdiction (from which no further appeal may be taken) to have resulted from the General Partner\'s fraud, willful misconduct, or gross negligence.
Line 365: **Section 7.5 --- Counterparts and Electronic Execution**
Line 367: This Amendment may be executed in any number of counterparts, each of which when so executed shall be deemed to be an original, and all of which taken together shall constitute one and the same instrument. Signatures to this Amendment delivered by facsimile transmission, by electronic mail in portable document format (.pdf), or by any other electronic means intended to preserve the original graphic and pictorial appearance of a document shall have the same force and effect as original signatures and shall be binding upon the parties. The parties agree that this Amendment may be executed and delivered by electronic signature in accordance with the Delaware Uniform Electronic Transactions Act, 6 Del. C. § 12A-101 *et seq.*, and the federal Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act, 15 U.S.C. § 7001 *et seq.*
Line 379: All notices, requests, demands, consents, and other communications required or permitted to be given under this Amendment shall be given in the manner and to the addresses specified in the Partnership Agreement for the delivery of notices. In addition, the following notice addresses shall apply for purposes of this Amendment:
Line 403: Each party hereto agrees to execute and deliver such additional documents, instruments, certificates, agreements, and consents, and to take such additional actions, as may be reasonably necessary or desirable to give full effect to the Reorganization and this Amendment and to carry out the intent and purposes hereof. Without limiting the generality of the foregoing, each Limited Partner agrees to execute such additional instruments as may be reasonably requested by the General Partner to facilitate the formation of the new entities, the Step 4 Contributions, the Step 5 Dissolutions, and the post-Reorganization structure.
Line 407: This Amendment may be further amended, modified, or supplemented only in accordance with the procedures and requirements set forth in the Partnership Agreement for amending the Partnership Agreement, including any required approvals of the Limited Partners and the LPAC.
Line 413: **IN WITNESS WHEREOF**, the General Partner has caused this Amendment to be executed as of the date first written above.
Line 425: **LIMITED PARTNER CONSENT**
Line 427: Each Limited Partner of the Partnership, by executing the Form of LP Consent attached hereto as Exhibit A or by otherwise consenting to this Amendment in the manner specified in the Partnership Agreement, hereby executes and agrees to be bound by the terms and provisions of this Amendment. The signature of each Limited Partner on the Form of LP Consent shall constitute such Limited Partner\'s execution of, and agreement to, this Amendment as if such Limited Partner had signed this Amendment directly.
Line 429: The General Partner is authorized to accept the executed Forms of LP Consent and to record the consent of each Limited Partner on the books and records of the Partnership.
Line 431: **[EXHIBIT A --- FORM OF LP CONSENT]{.underline}**
Line 433: **FORM OF LP CONSENT**
Line 439: The undersigned, being a Limited Partner of Solara Digital Partners Fund V LP, a Delaware limited partnership (the \"Partnership\"), hereby:
Line 443: > 2\. Consents to the Amendment and the Reorganization described therein, including the formation of the Consolidated Master Fund and the related feeder vehicles, the Step 4 Contributions, the Step 5 Dissolutions, and the post-Reorganization structure;
Line 447: > 4\. Agrees to be bound by the terms and provisions of the Amendment as if the undersigned had executed the Amendment directly.
Line 449: This Form of LP Consent is being executed in connection with the following fund vehicle(s) in which the undersigned holds a limited partnership interest (check all that apply):
Line 479: *A separate Form of LP Consent shall be completed and executed by each Limited Partner. The complete Form of LP Consent, including supplementary schedules and investor questionnaire updates, is contained in the engagement document suite maintained by Calderwood & Harkness LLP (Engagement No. 20250527-SDILP-PLR).*
Line 530:   April 22, 2025                      LPAC meeting; preliminary consent obtained (78% in interest voting in favor)
Line 532:   May 12, 2025                        Calderwood & Harkness LLP engagement letter executed
Line 540:   July 15, 2025 (Target)              LPAC review of final PLR Request
Line 557: *The General Partner shall provide the LPAC and the Limited Partners with periodic updates regarding the progress of the Reorganization and any material deviations from the foregoing schedule.*

